From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0247: AppleKeyStore: no lock assertions while locked

SpringBoard asked for the passcode never: after revoking authentication at
screen lock, -[SBFUserAuthenticationController _isUserAuthenticated] (auth
state 2) decides by taking an SBTransient MKBDeviceLockAssertion
(aks_assert_hold, 26) - "Checking if passcode locked", type GracePeriod - and
treats a granted one as "still in the grace period, authenticated". 26 always
succeeded, so a locked phone opened with a swipe. Refuse aks_assert_hold with
kIOReturnNotPermitted while a passcode is set and the bag is locked, as the kext
does (MKBDeviceLockAssertion maps 0xe00002e2 to its "locked" error).
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetKeyStore.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetKeyStore.cpp
index c30fe0a..482c0bd 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetKeyStore.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetKeyStore.cpp
@@ -1055,13 +1055,34 @@ AppleKeyStoreUserClient::externalMethod(uint32_t selector, IOExternalMethodArgum
 	case kAKSSetSystem:
 	case kAKSUnlockBag:
 	case kAKSLockBag:
-	case kAKSAssertHold:
 	case kAKSAssertDrop:
 	case kAKSAssertConsume:
 	case kAKSUnloadSessionBags:
 	case kAKSChangeSecretEpilogue:
 		args->scalarOutputCount = 0;
 		break;
+	case kAKSAssertHold: {
+		/*
+		 * aks_assert_hold(handle, type, timeout): scalars { type, timeout, handle }; types
+		 * (MKBDeviceLockAssertion's MKBAssertionKey) 0 Other, 1 RemoteProfile, 2 SBTransient,
+		 * 3 RestoreFromBackup, 4 TimeMachine. A lock assertion keeps an unlocked bag
+		 * unlocked; it cannot be taken while the bag is locked. SpringBoard depends on
+		 * that: after it revokes authentication (screen lock) it decides whether the
+		 * passcode is needed by taking an SBTransient assertion ("Checking if passcode
+		 * locked", type GracePeriod): taken = still in the grace period = no passcode.
+		 * Granting it while locked let a swipe unlock a locked phone.
+		 */
+		bool refuse;
+
+		args->scalarOutputCount = 0;
+		IOLockLock(sweet_aks_lock);
+		refuse = sa.has_pass && sa.locked;
+		IOLockUnlock(sweet_aks_lock);
+		if (refuse) {
+			ret = kIOReturnNotPermitted;
+		}
+		break;
+	}
 	case kAKSNotifyStateSet:
 		IOLockLock(sweet_aks_lock);
 		sa.notify_state = true;
